lon":35.49855,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[10]},{"id":"engedi_389","name":"Engedi","kind":"City","lat":31.46017,"lon":35.38899,"summary":"Fountain of the kid, place in the wilderness of Judah (Josh. 15:62), on the western shore of the Dead Sea (Ezek. 47:10), and nearly equidistant from both extremities.","verses":6,"v":[10]},{"id":"great_sea_493","name":"great sea","kind":"Water","lat":36.5802,"lon":17.11536,"summary":"(Joel 2:20; Ezek. 47:18), the Dead Sea, which lay on the east side of the Holy Land.","verses":12,"v":[10,15,19,20]},{"id":"hethlon_567","name":"Hethlon","kind":"","lat":34.73799,"lon":36.34092,"summary":"Wrapped up, a place on the north border of Palestine.","verses":2,"v":[15]},{"id":"zedad_1246","name":"Zedad","kind":"City","lat":34.31257,"lon":36.92548,"summary":"Side; sloping place, a town in the north of Palestine, near Hamath (Num. 34:8; Ezek. 47:15).","verses":2,"v":[15]},{"id":"berothah_179","name":"Berothah","kind":"","lat":33.93148,"lon":36.15205,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[16]},{"id":"damascus_322","name":"Damascus","kind":"City","lat":33.51161,"lon":36.3091,"summary":"Activity, the most ancient of Oriental cities; the capital of Syria (Isa. 7:8; 17:3); situated about 133 miles to the north of Jerusalem.","verses":55,"v":[16,17,18]},{"id":"hamath_516","name":"Hamath","kind":"City","lat":35.1359,"lon":36.7495,"summary":"Fortress, the capital of one of the kingdoms of Upper Syria of the same name, on the Orontes, in the valley of Lebanon, at the northern boundary of Palestine (Num. 13:21; 34:8), at the foot of Hermon (Josh. 13:5) towards Damascus (Zech. 9:2; Jer. 49:23).","verses":23,"v":[16,17]},{"id":"hauran_532","name":"Hauran","kind":"Region","lat":32.80008,"lon":35.9373,"summary":"Cave-land, mentioned only in Ezek. 47:16, 18. It was one of the ancient divisions of Bashan, and lay on the south-east of Gaulanitis or the Jaulan, and on the south of Lejah, extending from the Arnon to the Hieromax.","verses":2,"v":[16,18]},{"id":"hazer-hatticon_543","name":"Hazer-hatticon","kind":"","lat":35.1362,"lon":36.74949,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[16]},{"id":"sibraim_1092","name":"Sibraim","kind":"","lat":35.1362,"lon":36.74949,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[16]},{"id":"hazar-enan_537","name":"Hazar-enan","kind":"City","lat":34.2295,"lon":37.24008,"summary":"Village of fountains, a place on the north-east frontier of Palestine (Num. 34:9, 10). Some have identified it with Ayan ed-Dara in the heart of the central chain of Anti-Libanus.","verses":4,"v":[17]},{"id":"gilead_475","name":"Gilead","kind":"Region","lat":32.75,"lon":35.75,"summary":"Hill of testimony, (Gen. 31:21), a mountainous region east of Jordan. From its mountainous character it is called “the mount of Gilead” (Gen. 31:25).","verses":80,"v":[18]},{"id":"jordan_653","name":"Jordan","kind":"Water (River)","lat":33.18645,"lon":35.61916,"summary":"But besides these two historical fountains there is a third, called the Hasbany, which rises in the bottom of a valley at the western base of Hermon, 12 miles north of Tell-el-Kady.","verses":177,"v":[18]},{"id":"egypt_259","name":"Egypt","kind":"Water (River)","lat":31.03205,"lon":33.85496,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":8,"v":[19]},{"id":"meribah-kadesh_784","name":"Meribah-kadesh","kind":"","lat":30.68771,"lon":34.4948,"summary":"Holy, or Kadesh-Barnea, sacred desert of wandering, a place on the south-eastern border of Palestine, about 165 miles from Horeb. It lay in the “wilderness” or “desert of Zin” (Gen. 14:7; Num. 13:3-26; 14:29-33; 20:1; 27:14), on the border of Edom (20:16).","verses":3,"v":[19]},{"id":"tamar_1135","name":"Tamar","kind":"River","lat":31.02492,"lon":35.06415,"summary":"now Kurnub; from New Bible Dictionary","verses":2,"v":[19]},{"id":"lebo-hamath_723","name":"Lebo-hamath","kind":"","lat":34.19744,"lon":36.34204,"summary":"","verses":10,"v":[20]}],"events":[{"